Blockor is a lightweight, dependency-free daemon that protects FreeBSD and
OpenBSD servers from brute-force attacks. It watches your authentication logs
and blocks offenders through the PF firewall.

Features:
- Sliding detection window (findtime) and auto-expiring bans (bantime)
- IPv4 and IPv6 detection, banning and whitelisting
- CIDR whitelist
- Watch multiple log sources at once
- Notifications on ban/unban (syslog, email, or a custom command)
- Bans persist across reboots

It is a small set of /bin/sh scripts with no external dependencies.
